WEBVTT

00:29:28.454 --> 00:29:30.163
You know, it's like in my heart of hearts,

00:29:30.163 --> 00:29:33.996
I kind of knew it was more
likely not to succeed.

00:29:34.329 --> 00:29:36.579
You know, there's a lot of opportunity
cost for everyone,

00:29:36.788 --> 00:29:39.788
and it just seemed cleaner
to shut it down.

00:29:41.371 --> 00:29:43.704
Kathy wasn't just focused
on her own goals.

00:29:44.079 --> 00:29:45.996
She was thinking about
what was best for the

00:29:45.996 --> 00:29:51.371
team and coming up with the most honest
assessment that I could think would put

00:29:51.371 --> 00:29:54.371
the team as individuals in the
best position going forward,

00:29:54.371 --> 00:29:57.288
because no one wants to work on something
that's not going to work.

00:29:58.163 --> 00:30:01.329
Research shows that when we consider
our responsibilities to others,